  "answer_text": "Cato MFA tokens are time-based and valid in 30-second windows; a token generated within the same 30-second window will be the same across uses. On a trusted device (using the \"Don't ask me again on this device/computer\" option), MFA is not required while the configured token validity period is still valid and your geolocation hasn’t changed to a different country. Administrators can configure the MFA token validity duration in the authentication policy, and when a device is trusted that duration governs when MFA re-prompting occurs.",
